WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:04.700
Every year, Netflix ups the game with its
original content.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.030
In fact, the streaming service will soon boast
1,000 original movies and shows in its library.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.370
You'll probably never be able to watch them
all, but there's no denying that there's truly

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.520
something for everyone available.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:22.050
The company is already hard at work putting
out tantalizing glimpses of their 2019 lineup.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.380
From a gangster film by Martin Scorsese to
a brand new superhero series, 2019 is shaping

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.300
up to be an epic year.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.190
Here's a look at everything we know about
the 2019 Netflix originals that are sure to

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.090
blow you away.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.390
The Irishman

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.780
Barely five years ago, it would have been
insane to suggest that Martin Scorsese would

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.380
direct a direct-to-streaming feature.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:49.969
But now that video-on-demand services are
backing Oscar-winning films like Amazon's

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:54.720
Manchester by the Sea, it's safe to say that
the landscape has changed.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.260
And with Netflix willing to dump billions
in the pot for new original content, who can

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.940
blame Scorsese for working out a production
deal?

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:07.030
The result sees the Goodfellas director going
back to his roots with The Irishman, a mob

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:12.350
epic starring Robert De Niro as Frank Sheeran,
the hitman allegedly responsible for the disappearance

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.670
of Jimmy Hoffa.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:18.850
De Niro isn't the only big name attached:
Al Pacino is on board to play Hoffa, with

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:23.829
Joe Pesci, Harvey Keitel, and Anna Paquin
co-starring.

00:01:23.829 --> 00:01:25.799
The Central Park Five

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:30.649
With the hard-hitting documentary 13th, Ava
DuVernay proved beyond a shadow of a doubt

00:01:30.649 --> 00:01:35.350
that she could handle sensitive, real-life
struggles in a way that resonated with Netflix's

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:36.430
audience.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.710
So it should come as no surprise that the
streaming service is tapping her for an in-depth

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.899
dive into one of the most infamous crimes
of the '80s.

00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:50.189
In 1989, New Yorker Trisha Meili was jogging
in Central Park when she was assaulted.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:55.350
Police subsequently arrested five teenagers,
who were convicted and sentenced to prison.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:00.090
It wasn't until over a decade later that the
real perpetrator confessed, proving the five

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.759
young men to be innocent.

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:05.990
The Central Park Five will be a scripted drama
series that explores the aftermath of the

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:10.170
crime, from the media circus surrounding the
trials to the young men's eventual release

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.200
from prison.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:16.700
It should offer an emotional look into how
the case affected the lives of everyone involved.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.230
Sex Education

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.629
One of the bright spots of 2019 should be
Gillian Anderson's return to the small screen,

00:02:23.629 --> 00:02:26.740
after leaving both The X-Files and American
Gods.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:32.440
She's slated to star in Sex Education as Jean,
a therapist and working mom who's trying her

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.330
best to raise her son, Otis, who's a bit of
an odd duck.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.129
He's a virgin who knows more about getting
busy than any of his sheet-shaking classmates.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:46.860
Asa Butterfield, who you may know from Ender's
Game, stars as Otis, and the series is slated

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:50.019
for a tentative 2019 release date.

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:51.659
The Last Dance

00:02:51.659 --> 00:02:56.690
In the '90s, there was only one name that
mattered in basketball: Michael Jordan.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:02.269
As the scoreboard-stacking star of the Chicago
Bulls, Jordan became both an athletic legend

00:03:02.269 --> 00:03:04.629
and a pop culture icon.

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:09.400
He brought whole stadiums to their feet with
his buzzer beaters and rim-rattling dunks.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:14.299
With The Last Dance, Netflix is teaming up
with ESPN to deliver a one-of-a-kind look

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:19.790
at the sports climate of the early '90s, when
Air Jordan soared to stardom.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.870
The 10-part documentary series will combine
interviews with Jordan and his former teammates

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:28.870
along with archival footage of the Bulls'
final bid for one more championship in 1998.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:35.290
Put it all together, and it should be a unique,
enthralling experience for any sports fan.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.349
Polar

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:41.510
From Bond villain to cannibal genius, Mads
Mikkelsen has practically done it all, which

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:46.620
is why it's almost surprising that he's found
yet another exceptionally unique project to

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.620
tackle.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.760
Netflix's upcoming Polar is based on Polar:
Came from the Cold, a graphic novel that follows

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:58.329
a retired assassin who's forced back into
his old ways after an attempt on his life.

00:03:58.329 --> 00:04:02.790
The concept began life as a webcomic before
Dark Horse picked it up and turned it into

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.450
a graphic novel, and it's about as crazy as
you'd expect.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:12.230
From its hyper violence to its bleak, neo-noir
trappings, Polar: Came from the Cold is certainly

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.940
an experience, and we're hoping the film finds
a way to capture that insanity.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:21.510
Mikkelsen is taking the lead role, with Vanessa
Hudgens and Katheryn Winnick signed on to

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.360
co-star.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.360
Raising Dion

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:30.570
In 2015, writer and director Dennis Liu wrote
and released a comic book series called Raising

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.570
Dion, accompanied by a trailer to promote
it.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:39.250
The comic follows a single mother who realizes
that her seven-year-old son Dion is developing

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.250
superpowers.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.120
It's a unique, completely different type of
superhero story than many people are used

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.440
to, and the first issue snagged plenty of
fans.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:53.090
It didn't take long for Netflix to take notice,
ordering a ten-episode series with Liu at

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.090
the helm.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:58.550
The series will follow the same story as the
comic, with Alisha Wainwright starring as

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.520
Dion's mother, and Michael B. Jordan as her
husband.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.410
In a climate filled with superheroes of all
shapes and forms, Raising Dion definitely

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.540
looks like an original take on the genre.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.640
"Dion!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.100
You better not be naked up there again!"

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.820
Dolemite is My Name

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:19.570
Eddie Murphy has flown way under the radar
for the past several years, so it's big news

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.970
that he's set to appear in a new project.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:27.970
In Dolemite is My Name, he stars as Rudy Ray
Moore, a comedian and actor best known for

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:32.520
starring in the 1975 exploitation film Dolemite.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:38.090
Moore had a long, varied career in both standup
and the film industry, so there really isn't

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.280
a better actor to bring him to life.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:45.910
The supporting cast is just as star-studded,
with Wesley Snipes, T.I., and Keegan-Michael

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.590
Key all set to appear.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:52.310
Even Chris Rock was spotted on-set, decked
out in the kind of outfit that could've only

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.660
come from the '70s.

